      <div type="clause" n="2.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IEw">I Ew</ref> 2.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="140" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he ðonne nan riht næfde ne on boclande ne on folclande, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> se wære þe rihtes wyrnde scyldig XXX scll' wið þone cyning, ⁊ æt oðrum cyrre eac<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.3"/> swa, æt ðriddan cyrre cyninges oferhyrnesse, ðæt is CXX scll., buton he ær geswice.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="140" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.16"/> he ðonne nan riht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.17"/> næfde ne on boclande<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.14"/> ne on folclande<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.14"/>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> se wære ðe rihtes wyrde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.18"/> scyldig XXX scyl'<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.19"/> wið ðone cynnig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.20"/>, æt oðru<hi rend="italic">m</hi> cyrre eac swa, æt ðriddan cyrre cyniges<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.21"/> oferhyrnesse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.22"/>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> is CXX scyl'<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.19"/>, buton he ær geswice.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="2.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="141" ed="#liebermann"/>Si tunc rectum non habeat nec in boclánd<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.9"/> nec in folclánd<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.9"/>, sit ille qui rectum disfortiat reus XXX sol. erga regem; et altera uice item sic; ad terciam uicem ouerhyrnesse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.10"/> regis, hoc est CXX sol., si non cesset et satisfaciat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.11"/> antea.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="2.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="116" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif he ðonne nan riht næfde ne on boclande ne on folclande, þæt se wære þe rihtes wyrnde<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#IEw_2-1.attnote.fn.7"/> scyldig XXX scll' wið þone cyning, ⁊ æt oðrum cyrre eac swa, æt ðriddan cyrre cyninges oferhyrnesse, ðæt is CXX scll', buton he ær geswice.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="141" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn [Kläg]er aber kein Recht erhalten kann<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IEw_2-1.lnote.de.1"/>, an Urkunden-Grundeigenthum oder an volks[rechtlichem] Grundeigen, dass der [Verklagte], der das Recht verweigert hat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IEw_2-1.lnote.de.2"/>, 30 Schll. gegenüber dem Könige<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IEw_2-1.lnote.de.3"/> schuldig werde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IEw_2-1.lnote.de.4"/>, und beim zweiten Male ebenso viel, beim dritten Male die [Summe für] Ungehorsam gegen den König, nämlich 120 Schll.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IEw_2-1.lnote.de.5"/>, es sei denn, er stehe früher ab [vom Rechtsweigern].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">But if [the plaintiff] cannot obtain justice, concerning land held by charter or land held by folk-right, that the [accused] who has refused justice should become liable to the king for 30 shillings, and the second time as much, the third time the [sum for] disobedience to the king, namely 120 shillings, unless he desists [from refusing justice] beforehand.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="117" ed="#attenborough"/>If, however, he [the plaintiff] does not obtain his rights either in ‘bookland' or ‘folkland,’ he [the defendant] who withholds the rights shall forfeit a fine of 30 shillings to the king, and 30 shillings also on the second occasion, and on the third occasion the fine for insubordination to the king, that is 120 shillings, unless he has already desisted [from his wrong-doing].</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="141"><ref target="clause:Ine_8">Ine 8</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. Ine 8</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IIEw_1-3">II Ew 1.3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="195"><ref target="clause:IIEw_1-2">II Ew 1.2–1.3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="288"><ref target="clause:IIEw_1-3">II Ew 1.3</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">140</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Gif <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Gif Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">140</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-hte <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-hte Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">140</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-nd <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-nd Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">140</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wyrd <hi rend="italic">Ld; bessere</hi> wyrnde</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wyrd Ld; read wyrnde</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">140</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">scill. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">scill. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">140</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyning <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyning Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">140</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ninges <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ninges Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">140</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-nysse <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-nysse Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">140</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e <hi rend="italic">übergeschr. H</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e written above H</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">141</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-landa <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-landa T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">141</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-hern. <hi rend="italic">M;</hi> ouehyrnessam <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-hern. M; ouehyrnessam T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IEw_2-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">141</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">a. s. <hi rend="italic">Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a. s. Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IEw_2-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Durch des Beklagten Ausbleiben oder Unterlassen der Urteilserfüllung</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Through the defendant’s failure to appear or his failure to fulfil the judgement</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IEw_2-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Verallgemeinert II Ew 1, 2f.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Generalized in II Ew 1, 2f.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IEw_2-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ebenso Hu 7. Leis Wl 42</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Likewise Hu 7. Leis Wl 42</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IEw_2-1.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zu ergänzen bleibt aus Hl 9, dass der Klaganspruch daneben fortlebt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">It remains to be supplied from Hl 9 that the claim continues to subsist alongside</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IEw_2-1.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Ungehorsam’; <hi rend="italic">s.d. Gl</hi> 4. 18; Rückfall 6c. — Zu ergänzen ist, dass Kläger das Land zugesprochen erhält</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘Disobedience’; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 4. 18; Rückfall 6c. — It is to be supplied that the plaintiff is awarded the land</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IEw_2-1.attnote.fn.7" n="7" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">116</biblScope></bibl><label>wyrnde</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">wyrde</hi>. B. <hi rend="italic">wyrd</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
